\uline{Corollary} Let $\pi$ be a profinite group, a successive extension of free profinite groups. Then the centralizer \inserted{$\unsure{Z|\mathcal Z}$ in $\pi$} of any open subgroup $\pi'$ of $\pi$ is reduced to $\{1\}$.

By dévissage we are reduced to the case of a \uline{free} \inserted{profinite} group. \inserted{We know that $\pi'$ is therefore free.} We may assume $\pi'$ normal, and we assume that \unsure{the|its} center of a free profinite group is reduced to $1$.
\margin{to be checked}
Thus $\unsure{Z|\mathcal Z}\longrightarrow\pi/\pi'$ is injective, hence $\unsure{Z|\mathcal Z}$ is finite, and we assume that in a free profinite group, there is no element of finite order $\neq1$ --- which completes the proof.
